Build verified distribution archives

Usage: empack build [OPTIONS] [CONSUMERS]...

Arguments:
  [CONSUMERS]...  Consumers with a unique configured profile (or use --ad-hoc) [possible values:
                  modrinth, curseforge, prism, server, empack]

Options:
      --profile <NAME>                 Select complete authored profiles; repeat to build several
                                       together
      --ad-hoc                         Create consumer recipes from built-in defaults instead of
                                       configured profiles
      --explain                        Show effective profiles, overrides and recipient requirements
                                       without building
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>          Durable operation and recovery storage, separate from
                                       disposable caches [env: EMPACK_STATE_DIR=]
      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>          Disposable cache root; previews only inspect existing objects
                                       [env: EMPACK_CACHE_DIR=]
      --json                           Emit the effective build explanation as versioned JSON
      --delivery <DELIVERY>            How dependency bytes reach the consumer; independent of
                                       update authority [possible values: references, bundled]
      --environment <ENVIRONMENT>      Environment to project; each consumer validates the selected
                                       side [possible values: client, server, both]
      --updates <UPDATES>              Who may select future releases; requires a bound platform or
                                       publisher association [possible values: snapshot, platform,
                                       empack]
  -c, --clean                          Remove obsolete artifacts when the verified build is
                                       published
      --format <FORMAT>                Archive format override for distributions; mrpack and
                                       curseforge always use ZIP [possible values: zip, tar.gz, 7z]
      --downloads-dir <DOWNLOADS_DIR>  Directory to scan for manually downloaded restricted mods
                                       [env: EMPACK_DOWNLOADS_DIR=]
      --open-downloads                 Open verified provider pages for missing files after saving
                                       continuation
      --wait-downloads <SECONDS>       Wait for verified downloads, then present a fresh build plan
  -y, --yes                            Run without prompts; unresolved content choices still fail
                                       [env: EMPACK_YES=]
      --dry-run                        Preview changes without publishing project, instance or
                                       durable state [env: EMPACK_DRY_RUN=]
      --optional-defaults              Use authored defaults for optional files in materialized
                                       distributions
      --optional <CHOICE=true|false>   Decide one optional choice explicitly
      --allow-optional-metadata-loss   Allow reference archives to omit optional choice keys,
                                       defaults and descriptions
  -h, --help                           Print help
  -V, --version                        Print version

Consumers:
  modrinth    Modrinth archive with exact references and overrides
  curseforge  CurseForge client ZIP with exact references and overrides
  prism       Launcher instance using the selected delivery profile
  server      Prepared server runtime using the selected delivery profile
  empack      Exact native release and immutable assets

Without selectors, use build.default from empack.yml.
A consumer selects its unique configured profile; use --ad-hoc for a new recipe.
New projects and ad-hoc Prism/server recipes default to reference delivery.
Use --profile NAME when multiple profiles have the same consumer.
Use --explain (and optionally --json) to inspect the exact configuration without building.
Use --delivery references for a Prism/server snapshot installed by empack.
Prism/server reference exports and native empack exports need
pack.id and runtime.java settings.
Bundled content does not include client game binaries or imply offline launch.
Update authority is independent of dependency delivery; snapshots are the default.
All requested outputs are verified before combined publication.

Examples:
  empack build --dry-run modrinth prism
  empack build prism server --delivery references
  empack pending list
